WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:04.899
We’re ready?

00:00:04.899 --> 00:00:13.000
Putin's intervention in Syria, which was extremely
effective with very minimal damage to Russia's

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:20.930
treasury or blood expansion—casualties—has
shown the West that when the West creates

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:27.859
vacuum, when the West retreats from the self-imposed
red lines, again and again, Russia will exploit

00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:34.390
it and Russia will re-establish itself in
the areas where the former Soviet Union used

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:36.160
to be very influential.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:38.000
This is what I call the Putin doctrine.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:43.579
In fact, even in the official announcement,
it is clear that he's going to leave behind

00:00:43.579 --> 00:00:49.650
up to 800 soldiers, quite a few jet fighters
and jet bombers and special designation troops,

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:50.719
the so called Spetsnaz.

00:00:50.719 --> 00:00:52.870
There is no permanent withdrawal at all.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:57.820
When the U.S. withdraws, everything is emptied,
all the bases are gone, all the soldiers are

00:00:57.820 --> 00:00:58.820
gone.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:05.019
The lesson and the takeaway is that do not
leave a policy vacuum, a geostrategic vacuum,

00:01:05.019 --> 00:01:06.660
Russia will always jump in.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:10.579
So do you think Putin has withdrawn from Syria?

00:01:10.579 --> 00:01:14.029
Let us know in the comment section what you
think, and please let us know if there’s

00:01:14.029 --> 00:01:16.560
anything else you want us to cover in 60 seconds.

